   stage: Positive x follows fort-worth-runway's centreline in the takeoff direction, toward its departure end; y is right when facing that direction; z is height above the runway. The aircraft reference point is two metres above the pavement when its wheels are in contact.; x toward fort-worth-runway
   tone: Calm concentration and restrained anticipation.
   ambience: Open-air engine roar, increasing tire noise during the ground roll, and light wind; no music.
