== screenplay
AA-1: FIRST FLIGHT  (30 s; 3 scenes, 6 shots)
synopsis: Chief test pilot Jon Beesley pilots AA-1, the first prototype F-35A Lightning II, as it accelerates and takes off from Lockheed Martin's Fort Worth facility at 12:44 p.m. CST on December 15, 2006. With its landing gear extended, he tests the aircraft in landing configuration at 15,000 feet and 225 knots. He continues evaluating aircraft handling, the engine and subsystems. AA-1 returns to the runway and lands at 1:19 p.m. CST, completing its 35-minute inaugural flight.
theme: Measured confidence under exacting scrutiny.

1. EXT. LOCKHEED MARTIN’S FORT WORTH, TEXAS, FACILITY — DAY   0–8 s
   synopsis: Jon Beesley is inside AA-1 on the runway at Lockheed Martin's Fort Worth facility as the aircraft accelerates and becomes airborne. This is the opening of the prototype's inaugural flight.
   situation: At 12:44 p.m. CST on December 15, 2006, jon-beesley is seated inside aa-1 as it accelerates straight along fort-worth-runway and lifts clear with its landing gear extended; pavement, grassy margins, distant trees and raised ground surround the runway, and daytime sky is outside the canopy.
   stage: Positive x follows fort-worth-runway's centreline in the takeoff direction, toward its departure end; y is right when facing that direction; z is height above the runway. The aircraft reference point is two metres above the pavement when its wheels are in contact.; x toward fort-worth-runway
   tone: Calm concentration and restrained anticipation.
   ambience: Open-air engine roar, increasing tire noise during the ground roll, and light wind; no music.
   captions: [0s] "Fort Worth, Texas / December 15, 2006 · 12:44 p.m. CST"  [5s] "F-35A Lightning II"  [6s] "One engine"  [7s] "Conventional takeoff"
   line: jon-beesley and fort-worth-runway, extended along the runway centreline; camera side: On the runway centreline, looking back along it; neither camera crosses to either side.
